WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.910
Genetic disorders can be inherited in various patterns, including autosomal and sex, linked traits.

2
00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:19.530
Sex, linked traits are genes located on the sex chromosomes, with recessive traits requiring two copies to manifest in females.

3
00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:29.570
Males express X, linked recessive traits with one copy, while females require two copies to manifest the trait.

4
00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:38.770
Cystic fibrosis is an autosomal trait, not sex, linked, so options with III can be eliminated.

5
00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:47.150
The correct answer includes retinitis pigmentosa, color blindness, and Duchenne muscular dystrophy.

6
00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:57.210
Some forms of retinitis pigmentosa are X, linked recessive, while others may have different inheritance patterns.

7
00:00:57.210 --> 00:01:06.430
Use X marks the spot for boys to remember that males express X, linked recessive traits with one copy.

8
00:01:06.430 --> 00:01:14.890
Focus on understanding the inheritance pattern and eliminating options based on the type of trait.

9
00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:23.440
Refer to genetics textbooks for more information on sex, linked traits and inheritance patterns.

10
00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:32.110
Remember that X, linked recessive traits can manifest in males with one copy of the defective gene.
